Rebased onto current main — conflicts resolved next to #61875's new `activation_key=kMxfp8Dynamic` dispatch — and pushed the fail-closed fix promised in the Sep 17 comment:

- invalid e8m0 scales (0xFF) are rejected before conversion instead of propagating non-finite values;
- exact representability is verified per weight value (per-e2m1-code exponent-spread bound, aggregated on device, one host sync per converted tensor) and the load fails *before any layer parameter is replaced* — the byte-110 and byte-255 cases from the review now raise;
- the claim is narrowed to "exact for inputs accepted by the load-time exactness check", and the tests now cover both rejection cases, the spread boundaries, and the no-partial-replacement property.

@AranKomat the ROCm/V4.1 extension remains a coordinated follow-up per the earlier scoping — none of it is folded in here.

@mgoin @yewentao256 given #61875 landed while this was waiting: with Humming W4A8 available the remaining differentiation here is single-request TTFT / large-prompt prefill on stacks without humming-kernels (1.38–1.53× at 2k–8k input, at the documented 2× expert-weight-memory cost). Keep as an opt-in stopgap, narrow it, or fold into the W4A8 direction? Happy either way — the updated description now states the positioning explicitly.

